Track 2: Stationmaster Voss Misses Her Stop
- Story & Context: Lena Voss wrote this track after working a thirty-six hour shift at the Liège freight depot, deriving the lead arpeggio from the precise rhythm of an automated timetable board flipping its black plastic numbers. She mixed the track inside a sleeper compartment using a pocket synth plugged directly into a portable cassette deck while her tea grew cold beside her. The narrative follows an insomniac station clerk who deliberately ignores the arrival of the final train to stay inside the repetitive comfort of the depot's humming fluorescent lights. "The ticket punched a hole inside the hour," echoes her voice through a thick, gated delay loop over a minimal, driving EBM bassline.
